              "1.Warm- up: (3’)\nSing a song: Hello song\n*Aims: to create a friendly and active atmosphere in the class to beginning the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- Show the song on the screen.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tVlcKp3bWH8\n- Ask pupils to listen, sing and dance the song.\n- Say “Open your book page 7” and look at “Starter, Hello again!”.\n2.  Practice (30’)\nActivity 1.  Let’s sing\n*Aims: Ss will be able to sing the song “Hello. How are you?” with the correct pronunciation, rhythm and melody.\n*Procedure:\n- Draw pupils’ attention to the lyric of the song.\n- Have pupils read the verses of the lyrics.\n- Have pupils listen to the verses, check comprehension, drawing their attention to the pronunciation, rhythm and melody.\n+ Minh meets and greets Lucy on the first day of school.\n+ Nam introduces Mary and Mai.\n- Listen to and practise singing the song, line by line, while clapping their hands.\n- Ask pupils to listen to and sing the whole song while clapping their hands.\n-  Invite a few groups to the front of the class to sing the song.\nActivity 2.   Listen and tick:\n*Aims: Ss will be able to listen and understand a short text in which Ms Hoa greets the characters in the classroom and tick the correct pictures.\n*Procedure:\n- Draw pupils’ attention to the characters and check comprehension.\n+ Who is he/she?\n+ Where is he/she?\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_1/image1.png\" alt=\"image1.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n- Play the recording all the way through.\n- Play the recording and tick the pictures.\n- Tell pupils to swap their books with their partners, then check answers together as a class.\n- Have Ss to listen and repeat in chorus, sentence by sentence. Correct their pronunciation where necessary.\nKey: f (Minh); b (Ben); a (Linh); c (Lucy)\nActivity 3.    Let’s play\n*Aims: Ss will be able to spell some words learnt in Grade 3 by playing the game “Spelling bee”.\n*Procedure:\n- Before playing the game, have pupils look at the English alphabet and sing The Alphabet song or spell the letters of the song.\n- Tell pupils that they are going to spell some words they have learnt.\n- Explain how to play the game. Check comprehension and give feedback.\n- Write the words on a piece of paper or on the board.\n- Call a group of four pupils to the front of the class.\n- Give the piece of paper to one of group members and ask him/her to say on word (ex: friend). The other members spell the word (ex: F-R-I-E-N-D). The pupil who correctly spells the word first gets one point or star.\n- The pupil who has the most points or stars at the end of the game wins.\nDigital & AI mini-task: “Check the greeting!” (integrated into Activity 3 – 3’)\n- T displays three short teacher-prepared AI-style introductions: “Hello. I’m Ben.” / “Hello. I are Lucy.” / “Hello. My password is 1234.”\n- Ask pupils to choose the correct and safe introduction, correct “I are Lucy” to “I’m Lucy”, and explain why the password sentence should not be shared.\n- Digital/AI evidence: pupil checks language accuracy and privacy in one digital introduction.\n*Consolidation\n*Aims: Ss will be able consolidate and wrap up the content of the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- T asks ss to answer the following questions:\n+ What have you learnt from the lesson today?\n- T review the song.\n3. Homework. (2’)\n- Learn the song.\n- Prepare the new lesson: B.Classroom activities.",
