              "1.Warm- up: (3’)\nSing: Head, shoulders, knees and toes\n*Aims: to create a friendly and active atmosphere in the class to beginning the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- Show the song on the screen.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WX8HmogNyCY\n- Ask Ss to listen, sing and dance the song.\n- Say “Open your book page 42, 43” and look at “Extension activities”.\n2. Practice (30’)\nActivity 1.   Look and write\n*Aims: Ss will be able to identify five different countries in the pictures.\n*Procedure:\n- Have Ss look at the pictures and ask\n+ What do you see in the pictures?\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_10/image1.png\" alt=\"image1.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n-  Draw pupils’ attention to the pictures.\n- Ask Where is Viet Nam? and encourage pupils to point to it. Write Viet Nam on the board.\n- Point and ask about the other pictures: England, Japan, Australia and America.\n- Have pupils complete the activity by writing the name next to each country.\n- Check answers together as a class.\nKey: 1. Viet Nam    2. England\n3. Japan    4.  Australia    5.America.\nActivity 2. Look and write\n*Aims: Ss will be able to identify the different times in different countries.\n*Procedure:\n-  Have pupils look at the clocks.\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_10/image2.png\" alt=\"image2.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n- Draw pupils’ attention to the different times in different countries.\n- Write In America, it’s _____. on the board.\n-Read the first part of the sentence aloud and encourage pupils to complete it. When pupils answer correctly, write the answer on the board: 8:00 AM.\n- Have pupils work in pairs and complete the activity by completing the sentences.\n- Check answers as a class.\nKey: 1. 8:00 AM      2. 1:00 PM\n3. 7:00 PM      4. 9:00 PM\n5. 10:00 PM\nActivity 3.      Read the questions. Then tick the answers.\n*Aims: Ss will be able to read the questions and tick the correct answers, then say what countries are near / far from Viet Nam.\n*Procedure:\n- Draw pupils’ attention to Question 1 and read it as a class.\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_10/image3.png\" alt=\"image3.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_10/image4.png\" alt=\"image4.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_10/image5.png\" alt=\"image5.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_10/image6.png\" alt=\"image6.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n-   Ask pupils to look at Answer A with three answer options a, b and c.\n- Explain the new word Russia. Get them to look at the flags of Thailand, America and Russia, elicit the right answer and tick it (Picture a).\n- Repeat the same procedure with Answer B and question 2.\n- Get pupils to swap books with a partner, then check answers together as a class.\n- Write the correct answers on the board for pupils to correct their answers.\n- Have pupils say the answers by asking them Questions 1 and 2\nKey: 1. A. It’s Thailand. B. It’s Malaysia\n. 2. A. It’s Canada. B. It’s Australia.\n*Consolidation\n*Aims: Ss will be able consolidate and wrap up the content of the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- T asks ss to answer the following questions:\n+ What have you learnt from the lesson today?\n+What are the core values of the lesson? (if the teacher can take from the lesson).\n- T praises some Ss who are hardworking / active/ good…. as well as encourage others to try more.\n3. Homework. (2’)\n- Prepare the new lesson: Unit 6, Lesson 1 (1,2,3).\nDigital & AI mini-task: “Extension challenge – Check before you answer”\n- T displays a mixed review slide with country, clock and language information plus one AI-style mismatched label/caption.\n- T asks pupils to use the visual evidence to correct the mismatch.\n- Digital/AI evidence: pupil corrects one digital label/caption and explains by pointing to the clue.",
