              "1.Warm- up: (5’)\nGame: Slap the board\n*Aims: to create a friendly and active atmosphere in the class to beginning the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- Divide class into 2 groups\n- How to play:\n+ Each group chooses five Ss to play.\n+ Class will read aloud.\n+ Look at the picture, listen and slap the picture you heard.\n+ Who faster will get 1 mark.\n+ Which group with higher mark is the winner.\n- T gives feedback.\n- Say “Open your book page 47” and look at “Unit 6, Lesson 2 (4,5,6)”.\n2.Practice: (27’)\nActivity 1.   Listen and tick:\n*Aims: Ss will be able to listen to and understand two communicative contexts in which characters ask and answer questions about the quantity of school facilities, and tick the correct pictures.\n*Procedure:\n-  Elicit the word for the place in each picture\n-  Point at the pictures respectively to explain the context.\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_11/image1.png\" alt=\"image1.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n- T ask Ss to guess the answers.\n+ T writes Ss’guessing on the board.\n- Listen to the tape:\n+  Play the recording\n+ Play the recording again and get Ss to swap books with their partners.\n+  Play the recording again to check answers together as a class.\n+ Write the answers on the board for Ss to correct their answers. Then checks Ss’ guessing.\n-  Play the recording, sentence by sentence, for the class to listen and repeat in chorus.\nKey: 1. a        2. a\nActivity 2.   Look, compelete and read\n*Aims: Ss will be able to complete target sentence patterns in two dialogues with the help of picture cues.\n*Procedure:\n- Get Ss to look at the pictures and identify about school location.\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_11/image2.png\" alt=\"image2.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n- Give pupils complete the gaps in Dialogue 1, then have them compare their answers in pairs.\n- Ask some pairs to read aloud the dialogue.\n- Repeat the same procedure with Dialogue 2.\n- Invite one or two Ss to stand up and read the completed sentences.\nKey:\n1.\tmountains, one\n2.\tHow many, two, are there\n3.\nActivity 3.     Let’s sing\n*Aims: Ss will be able to sing the song How many …? with the correct pronunciation, rhythm and melody.\n*Procedure:\n- Have pupils read the lyrics to familiarise themselves with the questions and answers\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_11/image3.png\" alt=\"image3.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n- Have pupils listen to the whole song, drawing their attention to the pronunciation, the rhythm and the melody of the song.\n- Play the recording of the song once or twice for pupils to listen and repeat line by line and do related actions, ex: using fingers for numbers one and three.\n- Ask the to sing the whole song while doing actions or clapping hands.\n- Invite a few groups to the front of the class to sing the song. The class may sing along to reinforce the activity.\n*Consolidation\n*Aims: Ss will be able consolidate and wrap up the content of the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- T asks ss to answer the following questions:\n+ What have you learnt from the lesson today?\n+What are the core values of the lesson? (if the teacher can take from the lesson).\n- T praises some Ss who are hardworking / active/ good…. as well as encourage others to try more.\n3. Homework. (3’)\n- Practice part 5 again.\n- Prepare the new lesson: Unit 6, Lesson 3 (1,2,3).\nDigital & AI mini-task: “Count and check”\n- T shows a school-facility picture and one AI-style quantity sentence with a deliberate error.\n- T asks pupils to count and correct the sentence.\n- Digital/AI evidence: pupil uses visual counting evidence to repair one statement.",
              "- Ss read the words\n\n- Ss play game\n\n-Ss play game\n\n\n\n\n- Ss open their books\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Look at the pictures and say:\n+ Picture 1a. a school with a red building and a green building\n+ Picture 1b. a school with three buildings\n+ Picture 2a. a school with a computer room\n+ Picture 2b. a school with two computer rooms\n\n-Ss guess the answers\n- Ss listen to the tape and tick\n- Ss listen again, tick and swap books with their partners. \n\n\n- Ss check their answers and guessing\n\n\n-Ss listen and repeat.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss look at the picture and say\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss look and answer\n\n\n-Ss read aloud\n-Ss work in pairs and complete\n-Ss read aloud\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n- Ss listen \n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss listen and pay attention\n\n\n-Ss listen and repeat line by line\n\n\n\n\n-Ss sing the whole song\n\n-Ss sing in front of the class\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss answer the questions\n\n\n\n\n-Ss listen and clap their hands\n\n\n\n-Ss listen and take note\nDigital/AI pupil actions:\n- Ss count the facilities.\n- Ss correct one There is/There are sentence."
