              "1.Warm- up: (5’)\nGame: “Chant”\n*Aims: to review the vocabulary and structure about greet and respond to greetings.\n*Procedure:\n- Ask Ss chant and do the actions in Unit 6, Lesson 3 page 48 in groups.\n- Give point for the groups and encourage them.\n- Say “Open your book page 49” and look at “Unit 6, Lesson 3 (4, 5, 6)”.\n2.Practice: (8’)\nActivity 1.   Read and complete:\n*Aims: Ss will be able to read a paragraph about a school and complete four gapped sentences about its location and facilities.\n*Procedure:\n- Elicit and introduce the context.\n- Have Ss read aloud the words to fill in.\n- Model the first blank with Ss to make sure that they know how to do the task.\n- Give Ss enough time to complete the text.\n- Check the answers as a class.\n- Have Ss read the text aloud.\nKey: 1. village       2.  three\n3. garden      4. big playground\n3.Production: (19’)\nActivity 2.  Let’s write\n*Aims: Ss will be able to read, understand and complete a gapped paragraph about their own school locations and facilities.\n*Procedure:\n- Explain to the class the goal of this activity.\n- Have pupils to guess the missing information and complete the sentence with their own information.\n- Give pupils time to write their answers.\n- Get pupils to swap books and correct their answers in pairs.\n- Invite a pupil to stand up and read his / her completed sentences.\nKey:  Pupils’ answer\nEx:  My school is big. There are three buildings at my school. There is a big garden. My school has a playground. We can play football, badminton and volleyball there. I love my school!\nActivity 3.    Project.\n*Aims: Ss will be able to draw pupils’ schools and its facilities and present their drawings to the class\n*Procedure:\n-  Point at the sample drawing and explain that pupils are going to talk about the drawings of their schools including its location and some of its facilities.\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_11/image5.png\" alt=\"image5.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n- Have pupils show their drawings that they have prepared for the project.\n- Give pupils time to practise their presentations by themselves.\n- Give pupils some time to use their drawings to practise presenting in groups.\n- Select a few pupils to give their presentations in front of the class.\n- Get other pupils to give comments, and give corrections and feedback as necessary.\n*Consolidation\n*Aims: Ss will be able consolidate and wrap up the content of the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- T asks ss to answer the following questions:\n+ What have you learnt from the lesson today?\n+What are the core values of the lesson? (if the teacher can take from the lesson).\n- T praises some Ss who are hardworking / active/ good…. as well as encourage others to try more.\n4. Homework. (3’)\n- Prepare the new lesson: Unit 7, Lesson 1 (1, 2, 3).\nDigital & AI mini-task: “School picture – Check it!”\n- T displays a school picture/map and one AI-style sentence with a wrong location/facility detail.\n- T asks pupils to compare the sentence with the visual evidence and correct it.\n- Digital/AI evidence: pupil corrects one unsupported school statement.",
