              "1.Warm- up: (5’)\nGame: Slap the board\n*Aims: to create a friendly and active atmosphere in the class to beginning the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- Divide class into 2 groups: Tom and Jerry.\n- How to play:\n+ Each group chooses five Ss to play.\n+ Class will read aloud.\n+ Look at the picture, listen and slap the picture you heard.\n+ Who faster will get 1 mark.\n+ Which group with higher mark is the winner.\n- Say “Open your book page 51” and look at “Unit 7, Lesson 1 (4,5,6)”.\n2.Practice: (27’)\nActivity 1.   Listen and tick or cross:\n*Aims: Ss will be able to listen to and understand four communicative contexts in which pupils ask and answer questions about the subjects they have and tick or cross the pictures.\n*Procedure:\n-    Draw pupils’ attention to the pictures and ask questions: What subject is it?\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_12/image1.png\" alt=\"image1.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n-  Remind them to look at the book covers of the subjects and tick or cross the boxes while listening.\n- Play the recording all the way through.\n- Play the recording for pupils to listen and tick or cross the boxes.\n- Get pupils to swap books with a partner to check their answers.\n- Check the answer together.\n- Play the recording, sentence by sentence, for pupils to listen and repeat in chorus. Key: 1. v     2. x    3. v      4. x\nActivity 2.    Look, complete and read\n*Aims: Ss will be able to complete four gapped exchanges with the help of picture cues.\n*Procedure:\n- Get Ss to look at the pictures and identify the subjects in each picture.\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_12/image2.png\" alt=\"image2.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_12/image3.png\" alt=\"image3.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n- Have Ss look at the four incomplete sentences. Elicit and model with picture 1\n+  Ask Ss to read the sentence 1 in chorus.\n+  Ask Ss what word is missing in the gap (Vietnamese). Then have them complete the sentence (I have Vietnamese).\n- Have Ss work in pairs and complete the sentences 2, 3, 4.\n- Ask a few Ss to stand up and read the sentences aloud.\n-T gives feedbacks.\nKey:\n1. Vietnamese 2. have maths\n3. What subjects; science\n4. do you have; English; maths\nActivity 3.     Let’s play\n*Aims: Ss will be able to review the target vocabulary items using the puzzle, then ask and answer questions about the subjects pupils have at school.\n*Procedure:\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_12/image4.png\" alt=\"image4.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n-  Tell pupils the goal of the puzzle and how to play it. Then have them look at the spaces in the puzzle and given letters as well as picture cues to find appropriate lettersto complete the words.\n- Give pupils a time limit to do the puzzle individually.\n- Have pupils work in pairs. One points at the completed words or the clues and asks What subjects do you have today? and their partner answers I have ………\n- Invite a few pairs to the front of the classroom to ask and answer questions about what subjects they have today.\nKey: 1. science 2. Vietnamese 3. maths 4. English.\n*Consolidation\n*Aims: Ss will be able consolidate and wrap up the content of the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- T asks ss to answer the following questions:\n+ What have you learnt from the lesson today?\n+What are the core values of the lesson? (if the teacher can take from the lesson).\n- T praises some Ss who are hardworking / active/ good…. as well as encourage others to try more.\n3. Homework. (3’)\n- Practice part 5 again.\n- Prepare the new lesson: Unit 7, Lesson 2 (1,2,3).\nDigital & AI mini-task: “Timetable checker”\n- T displays a simple timetable and one AI-style subject/day sentence with a mismatch.\n- T asks pupils to find evidence in the timetable and repair the sentence.\n- Digital/AI evidence: pupil corrects one timetable statement.",
              "- Ss listen\n\n-Ss play game\n\n\n- Ss play game\n\n\n\n-Ss play game\n\n\n- Ss open their books\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Look at the pictures and say:\n+ Picture 1:   A Vietnamese textbook\n + Picture2:  An English textbook\n+ Picture 3:  A maths textbook\n+ Picture 4:  A science textbook\n\n\n\n-Ss listen to the teacher\n\n\n- Ss listen to the tape and tick or cross\n- Ss listen to the tape and tick or cross\n\n- Ss listen again, tick and swap books with their partners. \n- Check answer\n\n-Ss listen and repeat.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss look at the picture and say\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss look and answer\n\n-Ss read\n\n-Ss say and write\n\n-Ss work in pairs and complete\n\n-Ss read aloud\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n- Ss listen to the teacher\n\n-Ss play game\n\n\n\n\n-Ss play game\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss answer the questions\n\n\n\n-Ss listen and clap their hands\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss listen and take note\nDigital/AI pupil actions:\n- Ss check the timetable.\n- Ss correct the subject/day sentence."
