              "1.Warm- up: (5’)\nSlap the board\n*Aims: to create a friendly and active atmosphere in the class to beginning the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- Divide class into 2 groups: Tom and Jerry.\n- How to play:\n+ Each group chooses five Ss to play.\n+ Class will read aloud.\n+ Look at the picture, listen and slap the picture you heard.\n+ Who faster will get 1 mark.\n+ Which group with higher mark is the winner.\n- T gives feedback.\n- Say “Open your book page 63” and look at “Unit 9, Lesson 1 (4,5,6)”.\n2.Practice: (27’)\nActivity 1.   Listen and match:\n*Aims: Ss will be able to listen to and understand three communicative contexts in which characters ask and answer questions about sports days and match three characters with three correct pictures.\n*Procedure:\n-   Draw pupils’ attention to the pictures of the characters and the months.\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_15/image1.png\" alt=\"image1.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n-  Play the recording and ask pupils to listen and draw a line to match the character.\nEx: (Mary) with the month (Picture b).\n- Play the recording again for pupils to do the task.\n- Play the recording a third time to give pupils another listening opportunity if needed.\n- Get pupils to swap books with a partner, then check answers together as a class.\n- Write the correct answers on the board.\n- Play the recording again for pupils to listen and double-check their answers.\n- Play the recording, sentence by sentence, for the class to listen and repeat individually and in chorus.\nKey: 1. b     2. c      3.a\nActivity 2.    Look, complete and read\n*Aims: Ss will be able to complete four target sentence patterns in four exchanges with the help of picture cues.\n*Procedure:\n-  Have pupils look at the pictures and identify the months.\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_15/image2.png\" alt=\"image2.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_15/image3.png\" alt=\"image3.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n- Have Ss look at the four incomplete dialogue. Elicit and model with picture 1\n+  Ask Ss to read the sentence 1 in chorus.\n+  Ask Ss what word is missing in the gap (it is). Then have them complete the sentence (Yes, it is).\n-Have Ss work in pairs and complete the sentences 2, 3, 4.\n- Ask a few Ss to stand up and read the sentences aloud.\n-T gives feedbacks.\nKey:\n1. it is              2. April\n3. Is; May      4. in; No, it isn’t\nActivity 3.     Let’s sing\n*Aims: Ss will be able to sing the song Our sports day with the correct pronunciation, rhythm and melody\n*Procedure:\n- Draw pupils’ attention to the title and lyrics of the song.\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_15/image4.png\" alt=\"image4.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n- Play the recording all the way through.\n- Play the recording, line by line, for pupils to listen and repeat.\n- Introduce actions for pupils to do while they sing along with the recording.\n- Play the recording all the way through for pupils to sing along.\n- Put pupils into groups to make up their own actions for the song.\n- Invite groups to the front of the class to perform, while the rest of the class sings and / or claps along.\nKey:  1. red        2. blue\n3. yellow    4. brown\n*Consolidation\n*Aims: Ss will be able consolidate and wrap up the content of the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- T asks ss to answer the following questions:\n+ What have you learnt from the lesson today?\n+What are the core values of the lesson? (if the teacher can take from the lesson).\n- T praises some Ss who are hardworking / active/ good…. as well as encourage others to try more.\n3. Homework. (3’)\n- Practice part 5 again.\n- Prepare the new lesson: Unit 9, Lesson 2 (1,2,3).\nDigital & AI mini-task: “Sports-day calendar check”\n- T displays month/calendar cards and one AI-style sports-day sentence with a deliberate mismatch.\n- T asks pupils to check and correct it.\n- Digital/AI evidence: pupil uses calendar evidence to repair one statement.",
