              "1.Warm- up: (5’)\nGame: Who says fast?\n*Aims: to create a friendly and active atmosphere in the class to beginning the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- Hold a places card, then reveal it slowly.\n- Ask Where was you last summer?\n- Ask the Ss guess the answer as fast as possible.\n- Then have Ss do the same with the rest.\n- This can be played in groups to make it more interesting.\n- Say “Open your book page 71” and look at “Unit 10, Lesson 2 (4,5,6)”.\n2.Practice: (27’)\nActivity 1.   Listen and match:\n*Aims: Ss will be able to listen to and understand four communicative contexts about where someone was in the past and match the correct pictures.\n*Procedure:\n- Elicit the action of the character in each picture.\n+ Who are they?\n+ Which places are they?\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_17/image1.png\" alt=\"image1.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n- T ask Ss to guess the answers.\n+ T writes Ss’guessing on the board.\n- Listen to the tape:\n+  Play the recording\n+ Play the recording again and get Ss to swap books with their partners.\n+  Play the recording again to check answers together as a class.\n+ Write the answers on the board for Ss to correct their answers. Then checks Ss’ guessing.\n-  Play the recording, sentence by sentence, for the class to listen and repeat in chorus.\nKey: 1. d    2. c     3. a   4. b\nActivity 2.    Look, complete and read\n*Aims: Ss will be able to complete two gapped dialogues with the help of picture cues.\n*Procedure:\n- Get Ss to look at the pictures and identify the characters and the places in the pictures.\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_17/image2.png\" alt=\"image2.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n- Have Ss look at the first sentence and the pictures. Elicit and model with number 1: I was in London.\n+ Ask Ss read and complete the sentence.\n-Have Ss work in pairs and complete the other gaps\n- Ask a few Ss to stand up and read the sentences aloud.\n-T gives feedbacks.\nKey:\n1. London, Yes     2. Where, was, No\nActivity 3.     Let’s play\n*Aims: Ss will be able to review target words to make sentences about where someone was in the past by playing the game Making sentences.\n*Procedure:\n- Tell pupils that they are going to play the game Making sentences in groups of four or five.\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_17/image3.png\" alt=\"image3.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n- Nominate one pupil in each group as a leader.\n+ The leader says a sentence and the other group members have to stand in a line, holding the word cards to make a sentence. Example: Where were you last summer?\n- Have pupil work in groups to play the game.\n- Invite two groups to the front of the class to play the game.\n- Have the class give comments and announce the winner.\n- The group that makes most correct sentences will win.\n*Consolidation\n*Aims: Ss will be able consolidate and wrap up the content of the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- T asks ss to answer the following questions:\n+ What have you learnt from the lesson today?\n+What are the core values of the lesson? (if the teacher can take from the lesson).\n- T praises some Ss who are hardworking / active/ good…. as well as encourage others to try more.\n3. Homework. (3’)\n- Practice part 5 again.\n- Prepare the new lesson: Unit 10, Lesson 3 (1,2,3).\nDigital & AI mini-task: “Holiday place – Check it!”\n- T displays place/landmark pictures and one AI-style past-location sentence with a deliberate mismatch.\n- T asks pupils to compare with lesson evidence and correct it.\n- Digital/AI evidence: pupil corrects one past-location statement.",
              "- Ss listen\n\n- Ss play game\n\n-Ss play game\n\n\n- Ss open their books\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Look at the pictures and say:\n1. Mai 2. Bill 3. Mary 4. Nam\n+ Picture a. Tokyo Tower\n+ Picture b. Big Ben\n+ Picture c. Temple of the Golden Buddha\n+ Picture d. Opera House\n\n\n\n\n-Ss guess the answers\n\n- Ss listen to the tape and match\n- Ss listen again, match and swap books with their partners. \n-Ss listen again and check together\n\n- Ss check their answers and guessing\n\n\n-Ss listen and repeat.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss look at the picture and say\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss look and answer\n\n\n-Ss read and complete\n-Ss work in pairs and do the task\n\n-Ss read aloud\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss listen and pay attention\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss listen \n\n- Ss listen\n\n\n-Ss play the game\n\n- Ss play the game\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss answer the questions\n\n\n\n\n-Ss listen and clap their hands\n\n\n\n\n-Ss listen and take note\nDigital/AI pupil actions:\n- Ss compare the picture/audio and sentence.\n- Ss give the corrected past-location sentence."
