              "1.Warm- up: (3’)\nSing: Head, shoulders, knees and toes\n*Aims: to create a friendly and active atmosphere in the class to beginning the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- Show the song on the screen.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WX8HmogNyCY\n- Ask Ss to listen, sing and dance the song.\n- Say “Open your book page 76, 77” and look at “Extension activities”.\n\n\n2. Practice (30’)\nActivity 1.   Read and match \n*Aims: Ss will be able to read and match two reading texts with the pictures of city and country; distinguish the features of the city and the country.\n*Procedure:\n- Have pupils look at the Pictures a and b and elicit the features of them. \n+ What can you see in the city?\n+ What can you see in in the countryside?\n- Read text 1 aloud. Ask pupils to match text 1 to Picture a or b. Continue with text 2.\n- Get pupils to swap books with a partner, and check answers together as a class. \n- Write the correct answers on the board.\n- Have pupils underline the features of the city in text 1 and the features of the country in text 2.\n- Invite a few pairs of pupils to stand up and read the text aloud.\nKey: 1.b     2.a\nActivity 2.  Write countryside (a) or city (b).\n*Aims: Ss will be able to distinguish the features of the city and the country. *Procedure:\n- Check comprehention about this activity. \n- Do Number 1 together. Read the phrase in Number 1 aloud and elicit the answer (city). Have pupils write 1. city in the notebook.\n- Give pupils do the task. \n- Get pupils to swap books with a partner and check answers together as a class. \n-Write the correct answers on the board.\nKey: 1.b   2.b  3.a   4.a   5.b   6.b   7.b    8.a\n\nActivity 3.    Board game. Roll a dice. Listen and answer.\n*Aims: Ss will be able to revise the target vocabulary and sentence patterns by playing Board game.\n*Procedure:\n- Divide the class into four groups. \n- Each group rolls the dice in turn. On their turns, they move their game piece along the path according to the number of space by the dice.\n- When the groups land on a space, the teacher asks a question. \n+ The group gives the answer. \n+ If it is correct, they can stay in the box.\n+ There are some boxes like back to start, move ahead one space, miss a turn, move ahead three spaces, go back one space. \n- The game continues until one or all groups reach the “Finish” space.\n- Write the questions on the board. Have pupils sit in groups of three or four and repeat Steps 1- 4 to play in groups.\n\n*Consolidation\n*Aims: Ss will be able consolidate and wrap up the content of the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- T asks ss to answer the following questions:\n  + What have you learnt from the lesson today? \n+What are the core values of the lesson? (if the teacher can take from the lesson).\n - T praises some Ss who are hardworking / active/ good…. as well as encourage others to try more.\n\n3. Homework. (2’)\n- Prepare the first test.\nDigital & AI mini-task: “Review detective”\n- T shows a short digital review with 2-3 AI-style sample answers, including at least one deliberate error.\n- T asks pupils to compare answers with learnt patterns/picture clues and correct errors.\n- Digital/AI evidence: pupil identifies and corrects at least one inaccurate answer.",
