              "1.Warm- up: (5’)\nGame: “Passing the picture”\n*Aims: to create a friendly and active atmosphere in the class to beginning the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- T gives Ss a picture about some places\n- T asks Ss to listen to music and transfer a puppet around the class.\n- When the music stops, Ss who keep a picture have to practice with partner using:  I live………..\n- T gives feedback.\n- Say “Open your book page 7” and look at “Unit 11, Lesson 1 (4,5,6)”.\n2.Practice: (27’)\nActivity 1.   Listen and tick or cross:\n*Aims: Ss will be able to listen to and understand four communicative contexts in which the characters talk about where they live and tick or cross the correct pictures.\n*Procedure:\n-   Elicit the names of the streets or roads, and the house numbers\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_19/image5.png\" alt=\"image5.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n- T ask Ss to guess the answers.\n+ T writes pupils’guessing on the board.\n- Listen to the tape:\n+  Play the recording\n+ Play the recording again and get pupils to swap books with their partners.\n+  Play the recording again to check answers together as a class.\n+ Write the answers on the board for Ss to correct their answers. Then checks Ss’ guessing.\n-  Play the recording, sentence by sentence, for the class to listen and repeat in chorus.\nKey: 1.v     2.x      3.x       4.v\nActivity 2.  Look, complete and read.\n*Aims: Ss will be able to complete four gapped exchanges with the help of picture cues.\n*Procedure:\n-  Have Ss read the exchange and guess the missing word in the answer.\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_19/image6.png\" alt=\"image6.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n- Have Ss look at the four incomplete sentences and elicits the missing words in the sentences.\n- T models with sentence 1\n+ Ask Ss what is missing in the sentence.\n+ Have Ss look at the picture and complete the gap, then read the completed sentence in chorus.\n-Have Ss work in groups and complete the sentences 2,3 and 4.\n- Ask a few Ss to stand up and read the completed sentences aloud.\n-T gives feedbacks.\nKey:\n1. 35\n2. Tran Phu Road\n3. Where; 4 Thai Ha Street.\n4. live; in London Road\nActivity 3.    Let’s play.\n*Aims: Ss will be able to practise the target vocabulary and sentence patterns by playing the game Whispering.\n*Procedure:\n- Invite two or three teams of four pupils to the front. Each team makes a line.\n- Show a sentence to the last pupil of each team.\n+ Ask them to whisper the sentence to the next pupil.\n+ The pupil continues whispering until the one at the front of the line gets the sentence.\n+ The pupil at the front of the line shouts out the sentence or writes the sentence on the board.\n+ If it is correct, the team gets one star.\n- Play the game with other teams in the class.\n*Consolidation\n*Aims: Ss will be able consolidate and wrap up the content of the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- T asks ss to answer the following questions:\n+ What have you learnt from the lesson today?\n+What are the core values of the lesson? (if the teacher can take from the lesson).\n- T praises some Ss who are hardworking / active/ good…. as well as encourage others to try more.\n3. Homework. (3’)\n- Learn the vocabulary by heart\n- Prepare the new lesson: Unit 11, Lesson 2 (1,2,3).\nDigital & AI mini-task: “Review detective”\n- T shows 2-3 short AI-style review answers, including at least one deliberate error.\n- T asks pupils to compare each answer with a learnt pattern, picture or textbook clue and correct the error.\n- Digital/AI evidence: pupil identifies and corrects at least one inaccurate answer.",
              "- Ss listen and keep the picture\n- Ss listen to music and play the game\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss listen\n- Ss open their books\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Look at the pictures and say:\n+ Picture 1. A house at 12 Le Loi Street + Picture 2. A house in To Hieu Street\n+ Picture 3. A house at 15 Hoa Binh Road\n+ Picture 4. A house in Quang Trung Road\n\n-Ss guess the answers\n\n- Ss listen to the tape and tick/ cross\n\n- Ss listen again, tick/ cross and swap books with their partners. \n\n- Ss check their answers and guessing\n\n-Ss write the answer \n\n-Ss listen and repeat.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss look at the picture and say\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss look and answer\n\n\n-Ss answer: thirty-five\n-Ss say the missing word\n-Ss look, complete and read the completed sentence in chorus.\n-Ss complete the sentences\n\n-Ss read aloud\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss listen\n\n\n-Ss listen\n\n\n\n-Ss play the game\n\n\n-Ss play the game\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss answer the questions\n\n\n\n\n-Ss listen and clap their hands\n\n\n\n\n-Ss listen and take note\nDigital/AI pupil actions:\n- Ss check the sample answers with learnt language/picture evidence.\n- Ss correct at least one AI-style error."
