              "1.Warm- up: (5’)\nSing a song: “how are you”\n*Aims: to create a friendly and active atmosphere in the class to beginning the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- Show the song on the screen.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=O13gITUS5t4\n- Ask pupils to listen, sing and dance the song.\n- Say “Open your book page 9” and look at “Unit 11, Lesson 2 (4,5,6)”.\n2.Practice: (27’)\nActivity 1.   Listen and tick:\n*Aims: Ss will be able to listen to and understand two communicative contexts in which characters ask and answer questions about what a place is like and tick the correct pictures.\n*Procedure:\n-  Elicit the words and phrases to describe the pictures.\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_19/image10.png\" alt=\"image10.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n- T ask Ss to guess the answers.\n+ T writes Ss’guessing on the board.\n- Listen to the tape:\n+  Play the recording\n+ Play the recording again and get Ss to swap books with their partners.\n+  Play the recording again to check answers together as a class.\n+ Write the answers on the board for Ss to correct their answers. Then checks Ss’ guessing.\n-  Play the recording, sentence by sentence, for the class to listen and repeat in chorus.\nKey: 1.b    2. a\nActivity 2.  Look, complete and read.\n*Aims: Ss will be able to complete two gapped exchanges with the help of picture cues.\n*Procedure:\n-   Have pupils read the sentence and guess the missing words.\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_19/image11.png\" alt=\"image11.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n- T models with sentence 1.\n+ Have Ss look at the sentence.\n+ Ask them what is missing in the answer (81 Tran Hung Dao Street).\n+ Have Ss complete the gap.\n+ Have Ss read the completed sentence in chorus.\n-Have Ss work in pairs and complete the sentences 2.\n-  Invite pairs of pupils to stand up and read aloud the sentences.\n-T gives feedbacks.\nKey: 1. 81 Tran Hung Dao Street; quiet\n2. live; village; What’s; like\nActivity 3.    Let’s sing.\n*Aims: Ss will be able to sing the song My house with the correct pronunciation, rhythm and melody.\n*Procedure:\n-  Tell the Ss the title and the lyrics of the song.\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_19/image12.png\" alt=\"image12.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n- Have Ss read the first verse of the lyrics.\n+ Explain that the first verse is about a house in a town.\n+ Have Ss listen to the first verse, drawing their attention to the pronunciation, rhythm and melody.\n+Have Ss listen to and practise singing it, line by line, while making gestures for small, quiet and big\n- Explain that it is about a house in a city.\n- Ask pupils to listen to and sing the whole song while making gestures.\n- Invite a few groups to the front of the class to sing the song.\n+ The class may sing along and clap to reinforce the activity.\n*Consolidation\n*Aims: Ss will be able consolidate and wrap up the content of the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- T asks ss to answer the following questions:\n+ What have you learnt from the lesson today?\n+What are the core values of the lesson? (if the teacher can take from the lesson).\n- T praises some Ss who are hardworking / active/ good…. as well as encourage others to try more.\n3. Homework. (3’)\n- Prepare the new lesson: Unit 11, Lesson 3 (1,2,3).\nDigital & AI mini-task: “Review detective”\n- T shows 2-3 short AI-style review answers, including at least one deliberate error.\n- T asks pupils to compare each answer with a learnt pattern, picture or textbook clue and correct the error.\n- Digital/AI evidence: pupil identifies and corrects at least one inaccurate answer.",
