              "1.Warm- up: (5’)\nGame: Guessing\n*Aims: to review the vocabulary and structure about greet and respond to greetings. \n*Procedure:\n- Divide the class into 4 teams.\n- Look at the cards (1-8), there are pictures behind them. \n+ Let Ss guess the pictures then say aloud the job. \n+ Who can make it will have points for the team. (Spin the lucky wheel to get the points)\n- Encourage Ss to take part in the game and practice speaking English.\n- Give points for Ss.\n- Say “Open your book page 17” and look at “Unit 12, Lesson 3 (4, 5, 6)”.\n\n2.Practice: (8’)\nActivity 1.   Read and complete:\n*Aims: Ss will be able to read and show understanding of the text by filling in the gaps in the table.\n*Procedure:\n- Tell Ss about the context of the paragraphs\n- Point at the table and elicit the type of information they need to find in the texts.\n- Ask Ss attend to the blank in number 1 and find the missing word.\n- Write the missing word on the board and get the class to read the completeed sentence together.\n- Have Ss work in pairs and complete \n- Tell Ss to swap books with a partner, then check answers together as a class. \n- Write the correct answers on the board for pupils to correct their answers.\n-  Invite Ss to read the text aloud\n- T gives feedbacks.\nKey: 1. A nurse       2. At a nursing home\n       3. woker          4. At a factory \n\n3.Production: (19’)\nActivity 2.  Let’s write\n*Aims: Ss will be able to use the target language to complete a gapped text about pupils’ family members.\n*Procedure:\n- Explain to the class the goal of this activity. \n- Ask Ss to read each gapped sentence, guess the missing information and complete the sentence with their own personal information. \n- Give Ss time to write their answers\n- Ask Ss to swap and correct their answers in pairs. \n- Check the answers as a class.\nKey:  Pupils’ answer.\nExample: There are four people in my family. My mother is a nurse. She works at a nursing home. My father is a worker. He works at a factory. My sister and I are pupils. We study at a school.\nActivity 3.    Project.\n*Aims: Ss will be able to collect photos or draw pictures of family members at home and present them to the class by using the target language \n*Procedure:\n-  Explain that they have to show the photos / pictures that they have prepared at home and present them to the class.\n- Have Ss show the mind map that they have prepared for the project. \n- Revise some structures and vocabulary that Ss need for their presentations. \n+Example: Hello, everyone. My name’s Huong. I’m nine years old. This is my family.  There are four people in my family. My mother is a nurse. She works at a nursing home. My father is a worker. He works at a factory. My sister and I are pupils. We study at a school.\n- Give Ss time to practise their presentations by themselves. \n- Give Ss time to practise presenting their picture within their groups. \n- Select a few Ss to present their picture to the class if there is enough time. \n- Create a class display of the projects and organise a vote to find the most beautiful ones.\n*Consolidation\n*Aims: Ss will be able consolidate and wrap up the content of the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- T asks ss to answer the following questions:\n  + What have you learnt from the lesson today? \n+What are the core values of the lesson?\n- T praises some Ss who are hardworking / active/ good…. as well as encourage others to try more.\n\n4. Homework. (3’)\n- Prepare the new lesson: Unit 13: Lesson 1 (1,2,3).\nDigital & AI mini-task: “Review detective”\n- T shows 2-3 short AI-style review answers, including at least one deliberate error.\n- T asks pupils to compare each answer with a learnt pattern, picture or textbook clue and correct the error.\n- Digital/AI evidence: pupil identifies and corrects at least one inaccurate answer.",
              "- Ss listen \n\n-Ss play game\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n- Ss open their books\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n- Ss listen\n- Ss read and answer\n\n- Ss read and complete\n\n-Ss write the first word\n\n\n-Ss work in pairs and complete\n-Ss swap books and check the correct their answers\n-Ss write the correct answer\n-Ss read the text aloud\n-Ss listen\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss listen\n-Ss read and answer\n\n\n-Ss write\n-Ss swap books and check their answers\n-Ss check\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss listen\n\n\n-Ss listen and show the photos/ picture\n-Ss listen and pay attention\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss practice\n\n-Ss work in groups and say\n\n-Ss show the picture and perform in front of the class.\n\n-Ss vote the most beautiful ones\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss answer the questions\n\n\n-Ss listen and clap their hands\n\n\n\n\n-Ss listen and take note\nDigital/AI pupil actions:\n- Ss check the sample answers with learnt language/picture evidence.\n- Ss correct at least one AI-style error."
