              "1.Warm- up: (5’)\nGame: Whispering\n*Aims: to review the vocabulary and structure about greet and respond to greetings.\n*Procedure:\n- Divide class into 2 groups.\n-Ask 5 Ss in each group stand in a straight line.\n- T says a word or phrase to the first pupil in this line.\n- Then, the first pupil whispers what she/ he hear to the second person in line; the second one whispers what he/ she hears to the third one and so on until the last pupil in group hears the word or phrase.\n- The last pupil says the word or phrase out loud.\n- The faster group has correct word or phrase is the winner.\n- Say “Open your book page 36, 37” and look at Review 3.\n2.Practice: (52’)\nActivity 1.   Listen and number:\n*Aims: Ss will be able to listen to and understand four communicative contexts and number the correct pictures.\n*Procedure:\n-  Elicit what is shown in each picture.\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_26/image3.png\" alt=\"image3.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n- T ask Ss to guess the answers.\n+ T writes Ss’guessing on the board.\n- Listen to the tape:\n+  Play the recording\n+ Play the recording again and get Ss to swap books with their partners.\n+  Play the recording again to check answers together as a class.\n+ Write the answers on the board for Ss to correct their answers. Then checks Ss’ guessing.\n-  Play the recording, sentence by sentence, for the class to listen and repeat in chorus.\nKey: 1. c   2. a   3. d   4. b\nActivity 2.  Ask and answer\n*Aims: Ss will be able to ask and answer questions using picture cues.\n*Procedure:\n-  Get them to look at Mary’s thought bubble to identify what the girl looks like.\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_26/image4.png\" alt=\"image4.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n- Draw pupils’ attention to Nam’s question (What does your sister look like?).\n- Have Ss look at the girl in Mary’s thought bubble to answer the question.\n- Have Ss work in pairs to role-play the four exchanges.\n- Invite some pairs of Ss to stand up and take it in turns to role-play the target exchanges\nActivity 3.    Read and match\n*Aims: Ss will be able to read and match pairs of target sentence patterns\n*Procedure:\n- Draw pupils’ attention to the sentences. Point at Sentence 1, elicit the answer and give feedback. + Draw a line to match Sentence 1 with the letter d.\n- Give Ss time to do the task individually\n- Get Ss to swap books with a partner, then check answers as a class.\n- Write the correct answers on the board.\n- Invite some pairs of pupils to stand up and read the matched exchanges aloud.\nKey:   1.d    2. a     3. e    4. c      5. b\nActivity 4.    Read and complete\n*Aims: Ss will be able to read and show understanding of a text by completing the gaps.\n*Procedure:\n-  Draw Ss’ attention to the words in the box and the paragraph.\n+ Point at the first gapped sentence and have pupils read it aloud as a class.\n+ Elicit the missing word and give feedback.\n+ Complete the sentence and get pupils to read the completed sentence in chorus.\n- Give Ss time to do the task individually.\n- Get Ss to swap books with a partner, then check answers as a class.\n- Write the correct answers on the board.\n- Invite a few Ss to stand up and read the completed paragraph aloud.\nKey:1. factory 2. slim 3. works 4. pupil 5. watch\n3.Production: (10’)\nActivity 5.    Let’s write\n*Aims: Ss will be able to use the target language to complete a gapped paragraph using a picture cue.\n*Procedure:\n- Ask Ss to read the gapped text and fill in the gaps using the picture cue.\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_26/image5.png\" alt=\"image5.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n-  Write the sentence with the first gap on the board: My father ____.\n- Ask Ss to point at the father in the picture and encourage pupils to say what he does on Sundays (cooks meals). Give pupils time to write the answers.\n- Invite a few pupils to read the paragraph they have completed in front of the class.\nKey:     1. cooks meals 2. cleans the floor\n3. washes the dishes 4. clean the table\n*Consolidation\n*Aims: Ss will be able consolidate and wrap up the content of the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- T asks ss to answer the following questions:\n+ What have you learnt from the lesson today?\n- T praises some Ss who are hardworking / active/ good…. as well as encourage others to try more.\n4. Homework. (3’)\n- Prepare the new lesson: Extension activities\nDigital & AI mini-task: “Review detective”\n- T shows 2-3 short AI-style review answers, including at least one deliberate error.\n- T asks pupils to compare each answer with a learnt pattern, picture or textbook clue and correct the error.\n- Digital/AI evidence: pupil identifies and corrects at least one inaccurate answer.",
              "- Ss listen \n\n-Ss play game\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n- Ss open their books\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Look at the pictures and say:\n+ Picture a. a farmer                                  \n+ Picture b: a man playing tennis\n+ Picture c: a busy street\n+ Picture d: a tall boy\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss guess the answers\n\n\n- Ss listen to the tape and write number\n- Ss listen again, write number and swap books with their partners. \n\n-Ss write the answer and check their answers and guessing\n\n-Ss listen and repeat.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Look at the pictures and say\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n- Ss pay attention\n\n-Ss an swer the question\n\n-Ss work in pairs and role play\n\n-Ss role play in front of the class\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss read and match sentence 1\n\n\n-Ss do the task\n-Ss swap their books and check answer\n-Ss erite the correct answer\n-Ss read aloud\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss read the passge \n\n-Ss read the first gapped sentence\n\n-Ss complete and read aloud the completed sentence\n\n-Ss do the task\n-Ss swap books and check answer\n\n-Ss write the correct answer\n\n-Ss read the completed paragraph aloud\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss role play sentence 1\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss write the first gap\n\n-Ss point the picture and write\n\n\n\n-Ss read the paragraph in front of the class\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss listen\n\n-Ss listen and clap their hands\n\n\n\n-Ss listen and take note\nDigital/AI pupil actions:\n- Ss check the sample answers with learnt language/picture evidence.\n- Ss correct at least one AI-style error."
