              "Game: “Miming”\n*Aims: to create a friendly and active atmosphere in the class to beginning the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- Teacher divides the class into teams.\n- One student in each team stands in front of the board and faces his/her team.\n- Teacher writes/shows a phrase (stop).\n- The rest Ss mime the action written on the board while their teammate guesses the action and gives the answer.\n+ The team that gives the correct answer first gets one point.\n+ The team with the most points is the winner.\n- Say “Open your book page 49” and look at “Unit 17, Lesson 2 (4,5,6)”.\n2.Practice: (27’)\nActivity 1.   Listen and tick:\n*Aims: Ss will be able to listen to and understand two communicative contexts in which pupils ask and answer questions about directions and tick the correct pictures.\n*Procedure:\n-    Have Ss look at the pictures and ask questions to elicit the places and directions to the places in the pictures.\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_29/image7.png\" alt=\"image7.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n- T ask Ss to guess the answers.\n+ T writes Ss’guessing on the board.\n- Listen to the tape:\n+  Play the recording\n+ Play the recording again and get Ss to swap books with their partners.\n+  Play the recording again to check answers together as a class.\n+ Write the answers on the board for Ss to correct their answers. Then checks Ss’ guessing.\n-  Play the recording, sentence by sentence, for the class to listen and repeat in chorus.\nKey: 1.a           2. b\nActivity 2.  Look, complete and read.\n*Aims: Ss will be able to complete two gapped dialogues with the help of picture cues *Procedure:\n-  Have Ss read the dialogue and guess the missing words.\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_29/image8.png\" alt=\"image8.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n- T models with sentence 1.\n+ Have Ss look at the sentence.\n+ Ask them what is missing in the answer (the shopping centre).\n+ Have Ss complete the gap.\n+ Have Ss read the completed sentence in chorus.\n-Have Ss work in pairs and complete the other sentences.\n-  Invite pairs of pupils to stand up and read aloud the sentences.\n- T gives feedbacks.\nKey: 1. The shopping centre; left 2. How; right\nActivity 3.    Let’s play.\nShow me the way\n*Aims: Ss will be able to review the target vocabulary related to the topic “In the city” by playing Show me the way.\n*Procedure:\n- Divide class into two teams.\n- Have Ss look at the map listen to the teacher, fid the place and give the directions.\n- If a student’s answer is correct, the team gets one star.\n- After 5 minutes, the team that gets the most stars wins.\n- Have Ss in one team give direction, and the other team listen and find the place.\n*Consolidation\n*Aims: Ss will be able consolidate and wrap up the content of the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- T asks ss to answer the following questions:\n+ What have you learnt from the lesson today?\n+What are the core values of the lesson? (if the teacher can take from the lesson).\n- T praises some Ss who are hardworking / active/ good…. as well as encourage others to try more.\n3. Homework. (3’)\n- Prepare the new lesson: Unit 17, Lesson 3 (1,2,3).\nDigital & AI mini-task: “Review detective”\n- T shows 2-3 short AI-style review answers, including at least one deliberate error.\n- T asks pupils to compare each answer with a learnt pattern, picture or textbook clue and correct the error.\n- Digital/AI evidence: pupil identifies and corrects at least one inaccurate answer.",
