              "1.Warm- up: (5’)\nGame:  What’s in the box?\n*Aims: to review the vocabulary and structure about greet and respond to greetings.\n*Procedure:\n- Divide class into 4 teams.\n- Set rules: invite 1 pupil from each team go to the board look at the place\n(bookshop, bakery,waterpark,supermarket,cinema, …) then unscramble the words by writing on the board and say aloud what the place is. The fastest will get more points than the rest.\n- Encourage Ss join in the game.\n- Give points for the teams.\n- Say “Open your book page 51” and look at “Unit 17, Lesson 3 (4,5,6)”.\n2.Practice: (8’)\nActivity 1.   Read and tick True or False:\n*Aims: Ss will be able to read and show the understanding of the text by deciding if the statements are true or false.\n*Procedure:\n-  Explain that they should read the text and tick if the Sentences 1- 4 are true or false.\n- Do Statement 1 as an example.\n+ First, have Ss read Statement 1 and find what the statement is about (It’s about the bakery) and where it is (in Nguyen Hue Street).\n+  Then, find the information about the bakery in the text.\n+ Read carefully to decide if the statement is true or false.\n- Ask Ss to do the task independently.\n- Get Ss to swap their books with a partner and check their answers before checking as a class.\nKey: 1. True 2. False 3. False 4. True\n3.Production: (19’)\nActivity 2.  Let’s write\n*Aims: Ss will be able to complete a gapped text about giving directions.\n*Procedure:\n-  Explain that they should read the gapped text and fill in the gaps with their own information.\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_30/image1.png\" alt=\"image1.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n-  Have Ss do the first gapped sentence together as an example.\n+ Ask Ss to read the first sentence and elicit the words (ex: books, cakes, pencils). Then have them write it in the gap.\n- Give Ss time to complete other gaps independently.\n- Get Ss to swap their books with a partner and check their answers before checking as a class.\n- Invite one or two Ss to read their completed texts in front of the class.\nKey:    Pupils’ own answers\nExample: Today is Sunday. I want to buy some books. The bookshop is on Tran Hung Dao Street. I can go straight and turn right. The bookshop is on the left.\nActivity 3.    Project.\n*Aims: Ss will be able to draw a map and present it by giving directions to three places with visual aids.\n*Procedure:\n- Explain again that they are making a map of their neighbourhood to give directions from their house to at least three different places.\n- Draw a map, mark the directions from their house to at least three places on the map, and prepare how to present it at home.\n- Use Nam’s map and his presentation as an example.\n- Have Ss work in their groups. Each pupil shows his / her map and gives the directions from their house to three places.\n- Invite a few Ss to show the map and make a presentation in front of the class.\n*Consolidation\n*Aims: Ss will be able consolidate and wrap up the content of the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- T asks ss to answer the following questions:\n+ What have you learnt from the lesson today?\n4. Homework. (3’)\n- Prepare the new lesson: Unit 18- Lesson 1 (1,2,3).\nDigital & AI mini-task: “Review detective”\n- T shows 2-3 short AI-style review answers, including at least one deliberate error.\n- T asks pupils to compare each answer with a learnt pattern, picture or textbook clue and correct the error.\n- Digital/AI evidence: pupil identifies and corrects at least one inaccurate answer.",
              "- Ss listen \n\n-Ss play game\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n- Ss open their books\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss read and answer\n\n\n-Ss pay attention\n-Ss read statement 1 and answer\n\n\n\n- Ss find the information\n\n-Ss answer true or false\n\n-Ss do the task\n-Ss swap books and check the answer together\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss listen\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss read and answer\n\n-Ss write the words in the gap\n\n\n-Ss complete the gaps\n\n-Ss swap books and check their answer\n\n-Ss read their completed texts aloud\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss listen to the teacher\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss listen and pay attention\n\n\n-Ss work in groups to show the map and give the direction\n\n-Ss perform in front of the class.\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss answer the questions\n\n \n\n-Ss listen and take note\nDigital/AI pupil actions:\n- Ss check the sample answers with learnt language/picture evidence.\n- Ss correct at least one AI-style error."
