              "1.Warm- up: (5’)\nGame:  Let’s go shopping game (PPT)\n*Aims: to create a friendly and active atmosphere in the class to beginning the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- Divide the class into 2 teams.\n- Have Ss from each team choose an object they want to buy, then answer the question.\n-  If the Ss answer correctly, they get the points (coins) for that question to buy that object.\n- After 6 numbers, the team with the most points is the winner\n- Say “Open your book page 55” and look at “Unit 18, Lesson 2 (4,5,6)”.\n2.Practice: (27’)\nActivity 1.   Listen and number:\n*Aims: Ss will be able to listen to and understand four communicative contexts in which characters ask and answer questions about prices and number the correct pictures.\n*Procedure:\n- Have Ss look at the four picture cues and ask:\n+ How many pictures are there?\n+ What can you see in each picture?\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_31/image1.png\" alt=\"image1.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n-T ask Ss to guess the answers.\n+ T writes Ss’guessing on the board.\n- Listen to the tape:\n+  Play the recording\n+ Play the recording again and get Ss to swap books with their partners.\n+  Play the recording again to check answers together as a class.\n+ Write the answers on the board for Ss to correct their answers. Then checks Ss’ guessing.\n-  Play the recording, sentence by sentence, for the class to listen and repeat in chorus.\nKey: 1.c    2. a   3.d   4.b\nActivity 2.  Look, complete and read.\n*Aims: Ss will be able to complete two gapped dialogues about prices with the help of picture cues.\n*Procedure:\n-  Have Ss look at the picture in Question 1 and prompt them to ask and answer questions about the items and their prices\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_31/image2.png\" alt=\"image2.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n- T models with sentence 1.\n+ Have Ss look at the sentence.\n+ Ask them what is missing in the answer (fifty).\n+ Have Ss complete the gap.\n+ Have Ss read the completed sentence in chorus.\n-Have Ss work in pairs and complete the other sentences.\n-  Invite pairs of pupils to stand up and read aloud the sentences.\n- T gives feedbacks.\nKey: 1. fifty; thousand dong\n2. How much; seventy\nActivity 3.    Let’s play- Guess the price!\n*Aims: Ss will be able to review the words for prices and items at the shopping centre by playing the game Guess the price!\n*Procedure:\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_31/image3.png\" alt=\"image3.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n- Tell Ss that they are going to guess the prices of some items as quickly as possible\n- Put a picture card (example: a school bag) on the board.\n- Write a price range as a clue to help pupils guess the price (ex: 50.000đ – 60.000đ). Write the correct price on a piece of paper (ex: 55.000đ).\n- Ask How much is the school bag?\n- Invite some Ss to guess the correct price\n+ If anyone guesses correctly, show the class the piece of paper.\n+ Ask the class to read the price.\n- Play the game several times with different items.\n*Consolidation\n*Aims: Ss will be able consolidate and wrap up the content of the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- T asks ss to answer the following questions:\n+ What have you learnt from the lesson today?\n+What are the core values of the lesson? (if the teacher can take from the lesson).\n- T praises some Ss who are hardworking / active/ good…. as well as encourage others to try more.\n3. Homework. (3’)\n- Prepare the new lesson: Unit 18, Lesson 3 (1,2,3).\nDigital & AI mini-task: “Review detective”\n- T shows 2-3 short AI-style review answers, including at least one deliberate error.\n- T asks pupils to compare each answer with a learnt pattern, picture or textbook clue and correct the error.\n- Digital/AI evidence: pupil identifies and corrects at least one inaccurate answer.",
