              "1.Warm- up: (5’)\nGame:  Pass the ball\n*Aims: to review the vocabulary and structure about greet and respond to greetings.\n*Procedure:\n.- Divide the class into 3 teams.\n-  Each team has 1 sticky ball.\n- Play the music, Ss in each team take turns passing the ball.\n+After the music ends, 3 pupils who have the balls will stand up and say the model sentences.\n- Say “Open your book page 57” and look at “Unit 18, Lesson 3 (4,5,6)”.\n2.Practice: (8’)\nActivity 1.   Read and complete:\n*Aims: Ss will be able to read a paragraph and complete a table of information about locations and prices.\n*Procedure:\n- Have Ss look at the table of gapped information and guess what the missing information is, and what the paragraph is about\n- Ask Ss to read through the paragraph once or twice.\n- Ask Ss to look at the first gap in the table and encourage them to make a question for it (ex: What is at the bookshop?).\n+ Help Ss find out the correct answer (book).\n+ Repeat the same procedure with the other gaps.\n+ Allow Ss to do the activity independently.\n- Have Ss swap their books with a partner and check the answers.\n- Select a few pupils to read their answers in front of the class. Check their answers.\nKey: 1. book      2. behind the pet shop\n3. 50,000     4. ice cream\n3.Production: (19’)\nActivity 2.  Let’s write\n*Aims: Ss will be able to write a short paragraph about locations, items and prices at the shopping centre with the help of the suggested questions and an incomplete paragraph.\n*Procedure:\n-  Ask pupils to read the title, the given sentence and the questions, then look at the picture to get ideas for their writing.\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_31/image5.png\" alt=\"image5.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n-  First, have Ss read the guiding sentence.\n+ Then ask them to look at the picture to write a sentence about the location of the clothes shop.\n+ Next, let them write the answer to the question about the price of the skirt.\n+ After that, let them write sentences about the gift shop and the price of the pen.\n-Ask Ss to write the paragraph independently. - Get Ss to swap books with their partners and check their answers in pairs or groups before checking as a class.\nKey:    Pupils’ own answers\nMy mother and I are at the shopping centre. The clothes shop is near the bakery. My mother wants to buy a skirt. It’s sixty thousand dong. The gift shop is behind the clothes shop. I want to buy a pen. It’s thirty thousand dong.\nActivity 3.    Project.\n*Aims: Ss will be able to make a shopping list and talk about the locations and prices of certain items in front of the class\n*Procedure:\n- Explain that Ss are going to talk about the shopping list that they have made at home.\n- Have Ss show their shopping lists to their partner.\n- Give Ss some time to practise their presentations by themselves and in groups.\n- Select a few Ss to give their presentations in front of the class.\n*Consolidation\n*Aims: Ss will be able consolidate and wrap up the content of the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- T asks ss to answer the following questions:\n+ What have you learnt from the lesson today?\n- T praises some Ss who are hardworking / active/ good…. as well as encourage others to try more.\n4. Homework. (3’)\n- Prepare the new lesson: Unit 19- Lesson 1 (1,2,3).\nDigital & AI mini-task: “Review detective”\n- T shows 2-3 short AI-style review answers, including at least one deliberate error.\n- T asks pupils to compare each answer with a learnt pattern, picture or textbook clue and correct the error.\n- Digital/AI evidence: pupil identifies and corrects at least one inaccurate answer.",
