              "1.Warm- up: (5’)\nGame:  Choose and throw\n*Aims: to review the vocabulary and structure about greet and respond to greetings.\n*Procedure:\n- Divide class into 2 teams.\n- Call 1 pupil from each team to come to the board and throw a sticky ball at the answer.\n- Teacher marks the place where they throw it.\n- Teacher reveals the score for the correct answer.\n- Say “Open your book page 70” and look at Review 4.\n2.Practice: (27)\nActivity 1.   Listen and tick:\n*Aims: Ss will be able to listen to and understand five communicative contexts in which characters talk about familiar topics such as weather, directions, items price, animals and camp activities and tick the correct pictures.\n*Procedure:\n-  Elicit the words or phrases to describe the pictures in each option.\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_34/image5.png\" alt=\"image5.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n- T ask Ss to guess the answers.\n+ T writes Ss’guessing on the board.\n- Listen to the tape:\n+  Play the recording\n+ Play the recording again and get Ss to swap books with their partners.\n+  Play the recording again to check answers together as a class.\n+ Write the answers on the board for Ss to correct their answers. Then checks Ss’ guessing.\n-  Play the recording, sentence by sentence, for the class to listen and repeat in chorus.\nKey: 1. b    2. a    3. b   4. c     5. b\nActivity 2.  Ask and answer\n*Aims: Ss will be able to ask and answer questions using picture cues.\n*Procedure:\n-  Elicit the answer and give feedback.\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_34/image6.png\" alt=\"image6.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n-  Get Ss to role-play the exchange. Repeat the same procedure with the rest of the questions.\n- Give Ss time to take it in turns to role-play the four exchanges.\n- Invite pairs of Ss to stand up and take it in turns to role-play the target exchanges.\n*Consolidation\n*Aims: Ss will be able consolidate and wrap up the content of the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- T asks ss to answer the following questions:\n+ What have you learnt from the lesson today?\n- T praises some Ss who are hardworking / active/ good…. as well as encourage others to try more.\n3. Homework. (3’)\n- Prepare the new lesson: Review 4 (3,4,5)\nDigital & AI mini-task: “Review detective”\n- T shows 2-3 short AI-style review answers, including at least one deliberate error.\n- T asks pupils to compare each answer with a learnt pattern, picture or textbook clue and correct the error.\n- Digital/AI evidence: pupil identifies and corrects at least one inaccurate answer.",
              "- Ss listen \n\n-Ss play game\n\n\n\n\n\n\n- Ss open their books\n\n\n\n\n-Look at the pictures and say\n 1a. a rainy icon\n1b. a sunny icon\n1c. a windy icon\n2a. a ʽturn rightʼ road sign\n2b. a ʽturn leftʼ road sign\n2c. a ʽstopʼ road sign\n3a. a notebook and a price tag: 10,000 dong\n3b. a notebook and a price tag: 15,000 dong\n3c. a notebook and a price tag: 20,000 dong\n4a. Two giraffes\n4b. Two lions\n4c. Two hippos \n5a. Two boys taking a photo\n5b. Two boys putting up a tent\n5c. Two boys dancing around the campfire\n\n-Ss guess the answers\n\n\n- Ss listen to the tape and tick\n\n- Ss listen again, tick and swap books with their partners. \n\n- Ss check their answers and guessing\n\n\n-Ss listen and repeat.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Look at the pictures and say\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss role-play with the rest of the question\n\n- Ss role-play the four exchanges\n- Ss stand up and take it in turns to role-play.\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss listen and answer\n\n\n\n-Ss listen and clap their hands\n\n\n\n\n-Ss listen and take note\nDigital/AI pupil actions:\n- Ss check the sample answers with learnt language/picture evidence.\n- Ss correct at least one AI-style error."
