              "1.Warm- up: (5’)\nGame: Pass the ball\n*Aims: to review the vocabulary and structure about greet and respond to greetings.\n*Procedure:\n-  Play some music, Ss pass a ball around the class.\n- When the music stops, the pupil holding the ball stands up and say a word from the lesson.\n- Say “Open your book page 71” and look at Review 4.\n2.Practice: (27)\nActivity 1.    Read and match\n*Aims: Ss will be able to read and match pairs of target sentence patterns\n*Procedure:\n- Tell Ss about this activity. Point at sentence 1, elicit the answer and models.\n- Give Ss work in pairs to do the sentence 2,3,4,5.\n- Tell Ss to swap their books with their partners, then check answers together as a class.\n- Write the correct answers on the board for Ss to correct their answers.\n- Invite some pairs to stand up and read the matched exchanges aloud.\nKey:\n1. c       2. a          3. b      4. e        5. d\nActivity 2.    Read and complete\n*Aims: Ss will be able to read and show understanding of a text by completing the gaps.\n*Procedure:\n- Explain that they should read the text and circle the correct options to complete the gapped text.\n- Model sentence 1. First, have Ss read Sentence 1 and decide what information they need to find in the text and choose the correct option to complete the sentence.\n- Set a time limit for Ss to do the task independently.\n- Get Ss to swap their books with a partner and check their answers together before checking as a class.\n- Invite one or two pupils to read the text in front of the class.\nKey:\n1. sunny       2. playing\n3. dancing   4. photos\nActivity 3.    Let’s write\n*Aims: Ss will be able to use the target language to complete a gapped paragraph using a picture cue.\n*Procedure:\n-  Explain that they should read the gapped text and fill in the gaps with the information from a leaflet.\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_35/image1.png\" alt=\"image1.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n-  Have Ss do the first gapped sentence together as an example. Ask them to read the first sentence and elicit phrases (singing and dancing). Then have them write it in the gap.\n- Give Ss time to complete the text independently.\n- Get S to swap their books with their partner and check their answers.\n- Invite one or two Ss to read their completed texts in front of the class.\nKey:     Pupil’s answer\nEx: Welcome to our summer camp. We are doing a lot of activities here. The children are doing a lot of activities now. Some boys are near the tree. We are playing tug of war. Some girls are singing and dancing beautifully. They like our summer camp activities very much.\n*Consolidation\n*Aims: Ss will be able consolidate and wrap up the content of the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- T asks ss to answer the following questions:\n+ What have you learnt from the lesson today?\n- T praises some Ss who are hardworking / active/ good…. as well as encourage others to try more.\n3. Homework. (3’)\n- Prepare the new lesson: Extension activities\nDigital & AI mini-task: “Review detective”\n- T shows 2-3 short AI-style review answers, including at least one deliberate error.\n- T asks pupils to compare each answer with a learnt pattern, picture or textbook clue and correct the error.\n- Digital/AI evidence: pupil identifies and corrects at least one inaccurate answer.",
