              "1.Warm- up: (3’)\nSing: Head, shoulders, knees and toes\n*Aims: to create a friendly and active atmosphere in the class to beginning the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- Show the song on the screen.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WX8HmogNyCY\n- Ask Ss to listen, sing and dance the song.\n- Say “Open your book page 72” and look at “Extension activities”.\n2. Practice (30’)\nActivity 1.   Look and match\n*Aims: Ss will be able to match the animals with their correct homes.\n*Procedure:\n-  Tell Ss the goal of the activity and explain that they should match the animals with their correct homes.\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_35/image2.png\" alt=\"image2.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop4/tieng_anh/tuan_35/image3.png\" alt=\"image3.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n- Elicit the name of the animal in the picture. Then ask them to choose its home.\n- Set a time limit for Ss to do the task independently.\n- Get Ss to swap their books with a partner and check their answers.\n- Have Ss repeat the words nest, web, den, burrow.\nKey:1. c   2. a    3. d      4. b\nActivity 2. Complete\n*Aims: Ss will be able to complete four sentences to introduce the animals and their homes.\n*Procedure:\n- Tell Ss the goal of the activity and explain that they need to choose the animal homes in 2 to complete the sentences in 3.\n-Model number 1: Read the sentence aloud and elicit the answer (den).\n- Set a time limit for Ss to do the task independently.\n- Get Ss to swap their books with a partner and check their answers before checking as a class.\n- Have Ss repeat the completed sentences.\nKey: 1. den 2. nest 3. burrow 4. web\nActivity 3.       Board game. Roll a dice. Listen to a question and answer it.   *Aims: Ss will be able to review the target vocabulary and sentence patterns by playing Board games\n*Procedure:\n-  Divide the class into four groups.\n- Each group rolls the dice in turn. On their turns, they move their game piece along the path according to the number of spaces by the dice.\n- When the groups land on a space, the teacher asks a question.\n+ The group gives the answer.\n+  If it is correct, they can stay in the box. + Explain that there are some boxes like back to start, move ahead one space, miss a turn, move ahead three spaces, go back one space.\n- The game continues until one or all groups reach the “Finish” space.\n- Write the questions on the board. Have pupils sit in groups of three or four and repeat Steps 1-4 to play in groups.\n*Consolidation\n*Aims: Ss will be able consolidate and wrap up the content of the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- T asks ss to answer the following questions:\n+ What have you learnt from the lesson today?\n- T praises some Ss who are hardworking / active/ good…. as well as encourage others to try more.\n3. Homework. (2’)\n- Prepare the second term test\nDigital & AI mini-task: “Review detective”\n- T shows 2-3 short AI-style review answers, including at least one deliberate error.\n- T asks pupils to compare each answer with a learnt pattern, picture or textbook clue and correct the error.\n- Digital/AI evidence: pupil identifies and corrects at least one inaccurate answer.",
